# E2 arm 9, Leaseholder, in the discriminating scenario (24 session trees on weka-x32-long): the full arm, its knob
# (the critical-window budget of predicted background prefill: 0, 150 and 500 ms), and one run of each single-mechanism
# ablation. The gateway runs policy leaseholder, the engine the make-room variant, the voice worker posts lifecycle
# events, each unless the point turns it off. Grouped by engine, so the engine restarts five times.
#   benchmarks/e2/campaign.sh benchmarks/e2/a9.campaign

# The make-room engine as arm 9 runs it
arms/disc-a9-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-budget0-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-budget500-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-no-throttle-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-no-headroom-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-no-degrade-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-trigger-request-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-no-events-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-engine-only-s24.toml

# make-room with one of its switches off
arms/disc-a9-no-kv-makeroom-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-no-budget-cap-s24.toml
arms/disc-a9-no-reserve-s24.toml

# The gateway policy on the frozen engine
arms/disc-a9-gateway-only-s24.toml
